Package: bbssr
Type: Package
Title: Blinded Sample Size Re-Estimation for Binary Endpoints
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: person("Gosuke", "Homma", email = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com", 
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for blinded sample size re-estimation (BSSR) in two-arm clinical 
    trials with binary endpoints, together with the exact power and sample size 
    calculations that the re-estimation relies on. Seven statistical tests are 
    implemented: Pearson chi-squared, Fisher exact, Fisher mid-p, Z-pooled exact 
    unconditional, the exact unconditional test of Boschloo (1970) 
    <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9574.1970.tb00104.x>, and the tests of non-inferiority of 
    Blackwelder (1982) <doi:10.1016/0197-2456(82)90024-1> and of Farrington and 
    Manning (1990) <doi:10.1002/sim.4780091208>, with a margin on the scale of the risk 
    difference or the risk ratio. Each test is available with a 
    one-sided or a two-sided alternative, and the exact unconditional tests can be 
    combined with the Berger-Boos procedure. The power, the distribution of the final 
    sample size and the type I error rate of a re-estimation design are computed 
    exactly, the significance level can be adjusted so that the type I error rate is 
    controlled, and the sample size can be re-estimated from the blinded data of a 
    trial that is under way. Statistical methods based on Mehrotra et al. (2003) 
    <doi:10.1111/1541-0420.00051>, Berger and Boos (1994) 
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1994.10476836>, Friede and Kieser (2004) 
    <doi:10.1002/pst.140>, Friede et al. (2007) <doi:10.1002/bimj.200610373> and 
    Kieser (2020) <doi:10.1007/978-3-030-49528-2_21>.
